 All notable changes to Yakherd are recorded here.
 
+## Source instruction pack - 2026-09-24 (not an installer release)
+
+- Establishes `docs/SSOT_PROCESS.md` as the current product-repository process,
+  with self-contained AGENTS/SSOT/BASELINE/NOW/README starters and a direct
+  new-repository entry point.
+- Defaults to one implementation task, artifact-based independent review and
+  evidence-backed milestone transitions; removes mandatory startup role
+  rosters and review ledgers from the new instruction path.
+- Adds an explicit migration guide and a stopped-TRAVOLTA steering prompt
+  that preserves product requirements, research, provenance and real hazards.
+- Marks the packaged five-role installer as legacy. Package behavior, version,
+  manifest/release bindings and existing installations are unchanged. This
+  source pack does not claim compatibility with the legacy protocol validator;
+  adopting it requires explicit instruction migration, not an installer rerun.
+
+## 1.5.0 - 2026-07-28
+
+- Replaces the global two-failure review stop with a finite strict-work ledger:
+  `R0 -> C1 -> C2 -> PASS | HUMAN_DISPOSITION_REQUIRED`.
+- Keeps repairs bounded to the accepted write set and authority, prevents
+  renamed/forked review-budget resets, and allows a distinct blocker discovered
+  during correction to use only the remaining repair wave.
+- Treats one unchanged-candidate evidence rerun as a bounded verification
+  action, not new authority or review budget.
+- Records a deferred, standard-library-only strict-review ledger validator as
+  hardening work; it is not a prerequisite for the proportional rule.
+
